    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1189">

                <pb facs="0974" n="858" xml:id="pg858"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/5293.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-10-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 20, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s October 19, 5 p.m. I have found no excitement concerning arrival of
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Des Moines</hi> except on the part of
                    administration, and I so informed Minister for Foreign Affairs just now. He
                    declared that the Government had no objection to the arrival of the vessel now,
                    but that there had been fears as to the effect which its arrival would have at
                    the outbreak of uprising at Vera Cruz.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schuyler.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
